<title>SWEDEN: Saab Auto U.S. Sept car sales up 26 pct.</title>
<headline>Saab Auto U.S. Sept car sales up 26 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish car manufacturer Saab Automobile said on Wednesday its car sales in the United States had increased by 26 percent to 2,874 vehicles in September.</p>
<p>Sales over the the first nine months of the year rose by 11 percent to 22,575 cars, Saab Automobile said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company is owned by Swedish investment group Investor and the U.S. General Motors.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1006</p>
